14. Privacy and data collection

14.1 When Your App runs the SDK Binaries, they collect and send to the Service the data
described in the Documentation and declared in the privacy manifests published with the SDK
Binaries, in accordance with the consent state that Your App sets through the SDK Binaries.

14.2 You are responsible for:
(a) giving End Users the notices, and obtaining the consents, that applicable law requires
for the data that Your App, including the SDK Binaries, collects;
(b) setting the consent state in the SDK Binaries accordingly;
(c) the accuracy of the privacy disclosures you make for Your App, including in App Store
Connect and in the Google Play Data safety form;
(d) not passing to the SDK Binaries, as an account key or other value, information that
directly identifies an End User, such as an e-mail address or a telephone number, except as
the Documentation allows; and
(e) deciding whether you may use the SDK Binaries in Your App if it is directed at children.
HELPERG has not assessed the SDK Binaries for apps directed at children, for Apple's Kids
category or for Google Play's Families program, and makes no statement that they meet those
requirements.

14.3 Data that the Service receives from Your App is processed under the Service Terms and,
where you and HELPERG have signed one, a DPA. If your use of the Service requires a data
processing agreement, you are responsible for concluding one with HELPERG before you send
personal data to the Service; HELPERG's data-processing page explains how to request one.

15. Updates; no support or service levels

15.1 HELPERG may publish new versions of the SDK Binaries but is not required to. A published
version is never changed; a correction is published as a new version.

15.2 This Agreement includes no obligation to provide support, maintenance, updates, security
fixes, availability or any service level for the SDK Binaries. Support or a service level
exists only where HELPERG has agreed to it in writing for your WebmasterID account.

15.3 Each version of the SDK Binaries is governed by the version of this Agreement published
with it.

16. Term and termination

16.1 This Agreement applies from your acceptance until it is terminated.

16.2 You may terminate this Agreement at any time by ceasing to use and distribute the SDK
Binaries.

16.3 HELPERG may terminate this Agreement by written notice if you materially breach it and
do not cure the breach within thirty (30) days after the notice, or immediately if the breach
cannot be cured or concerns section 5(f), section 5(g), section 20 or section 21.

16.4 After termination:
(a) you must not add the SDK Binaries to a new application, or to a version of Your App
released more than 90 days after termination;
(b) during that period you may continue to distribute versions of Your App released before
termination;
(c) you are not required to recall, disable or remove copies of Your App that End Users have
already installed, and End Users may continue to use them; and
(d) termination of this Agreement does not by itself oblige HELPERG to keep accepting data
from the SDK Binaries in Your App; the Service Terms govern your use of the Service.
Where termination is for a breach of section 20, distribution that the laws referred to there
prohibit must stop immediately.

16.5 Sections 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16.4, 17, 18, 19, 20, 22, 23 and 24 survive
termination.

