23. Order of precedence; general

23.1 Order of precedence.
(a) For the SDK Binaries — the license, its conditions and restrictions, and the rights in
them — this Agreement governs.
(b) For the Service — your account, plans, fees and limits, and the processing of the data
that the Service receives — the Service Terms govern, and for personal data a DPA governs
where one exists.
(c) If a provision of this Agreement and a provision of the Service Terms cannot both be
complied with, the document that governs the subject under (a) or (b) prevails.
(d) For the SDK Binaries, this Agreement is HELPERG's permission under section 3 of the
Service Terms to redistribute them as this Agreement allows; and section 8 applies to the
SDK Binaries notwithstanding any restriction on reverse engineering in the Service Terms.

23.2 Entire agreement. This Agreement, together with the documents it refers to, is the
entire agreement between you and HELPERG about the SDK Binaries and supersedes any prior
understanding about them.

23.3 Severability. If any provision of this Agreement is held invalid or unenforceable,
it will be enforced to the maximum extent permissible, and the remaining provisions remain
in full force and effect.

23.4 Assignment. You may not assign or transfer this Agreement without HELPERG's prior
written consent, except to a successor to all or substantially all of the business or assets
relating to Your App. HELPERG may assign this Agreement to an affiliate or to a successor to
the business of the Service. Any other assignment is void.

23.5 No waiver. A failure or delay in enforcing a provision is not a waiver of it.

23.6 Notices. Notices to HELPERG must be sent to the contact address given in section 10
of the Service Terms, or by post to HELPERG's address above. HELPERG may give you notice
through the WebmasterID account associated with Your App, by e-mail to its account address,
or by publication in the SDK Binaries' release notes.

23.7 Relationship. The parties are independent contractors. This Agreement creates no
partnership, agency or employment relationship and no third-party beneficiary rights.

23.8 Government end users. The SDK Binaries are "commercial computer software" and are
provided to government end users only with the rights granted to all other licensees under
this Agreement.

23.9 Language. This Agreement is written in English. A translation is provided for
convenience only; the English version controls.

